 7:46\" href=\"/I_Kings.7.46\">1 K 7:46</a> cf. <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 4:17\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.4.17\">2 Ch 4:17</a> (<em>firmness of earth</em>, firm earth, clay-ground, for casting-moulds; or <em>clay-moulds</em> (Be)? or is this n.pr.? Klo proposes <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּמְּעָרָה הָאֲדֻמָּה</span> <em>in the red cave</em>); mule-loads of <a data-ref=\"II Kings 5:17\" href=\"/II_Kings.5.17\">2 K 5:17</a>; in it lie the dead <span dir=\"rtl\">מִיְּשֵׁנֵי אַדְמַת־עָפָר</span> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 12:2\" href=\"/Daniel.12.2\">Dn 12:2</a> cf. <a data-ref=\"Genesis 3:19\" href=\"/Genesis.3.19\">Gn 3:19</a>, <a data-ref=\"Genesis 3:23\" href=\"/Genesis.3.23\">23</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 146:4\" href=\"/Psalms.146.4\">ψ 146:4</a>."}],"all_cited":true,"num":"3."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>ground</em> as earth’s visible surface; <span dir=\"rtl\">רֶמֶס הָא׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Genesis 1:25\" href=\"/Genesis.1.25\">Gn 1:25</a>; <a data-ref=\"Genesis 6:20\" href=\"/Genesis.6.20\">6:20</a> (both P) <a data-ref=\"Hosea 2:20\" href=\"/Hosea.2.20\">Ho 2:20</a> cf. <a data-ref=\"Genesis 7:8\" href=\"/Genesis.7.8\">Gn 7:8</a>; <a data-ref=\"Genesis 9:2\" href=\"/Genesis.9.2\">9:2</a> (J?) <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 20:25\" href=\"/Leviticus.20.25\">Lv 20:25</a> (P) <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 4:18\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.4.18\">Dt 4:18</a> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 38:20\" href=\"/Ezekiel.38.20\">Ez 38:20</a>; also <a data-ref=\"Genesis 4:10\" href=\"/Genesis.4.10\">Gn 4:10</a> (J) <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 24:21\" href=\"/Isaiah.24.21\">Is 24:21</a> <a data-ref=\"Amos 3:5\" href=\"/Amos.3.5\">Am 3:5</a> <a data-ref=\"Zephaniah 1:2\" href=\"/Zephaniah.1.2\">Zp 1:2</a>, <a data-ref=\"Zephaniah 1:3\" href=\"/Zephaniah.1.3\">3</a>; as wet with dew <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 17:12\" href=\"/II_Samuel.17.12\">2 S 17:12</a>; rain <a data-ref=\"I Kings 17:14\" href=\"/I_Kings.17.14\">1 K 17:14</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 18:1\" href=\"/I_Kings.18.1\">18:1</a>; cf. personif. <span dir=\"rtl\">פָּ